From: HbbTV2 experiment <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] GLContext: fall back to a pbuffer context when EGL has no surfaceless support

The web process creates its offscreen contexts (the compositor's, Skia's, the sharing context) with GLContext::createOffscreen(). For a
PlatformDisplay of type Surfaceless or Default (patch 0004) that means createSurfacelessContext(), which needs EGL_KHR_surfaceless_context
or EGL_KHR_surfaceless_opengl, and createOffscreenContext() deliberately does not fall back to a pbuffer for that target.

The Broadcom/Nexus V3D driver of the VU+ Ultimo 4K (libv3ddriver.so from libgles-vuultimo4k-17.1) advertises neither: its EGL extensions are
only KHR_image(_base/_pixmap), KHR_vg_parent_image, KHR_gl_texture_2D/cubemap_image, KHR_lock_surface and KHR_fence_sync (and it is GLES 2.0
only). No context could be created, PlatformDisplay::skiaGLContext() returned null and AcceleratedSurface dereferenced it, GL calls ran
without a current context: the web process died with a SIGSEGV, silently (WEB PROCESS TERMINATED, nothing in dmesg), right after the Nexus
join/register of patch 0017.

- createOffscreenContext(): for Target::Surfaceless, when the EGL implementation really has no surfaceless support, continue to the existing
  pbuffer fallback (createPbufferContext(): a 1x1 pbuffer surface, everything is rendered into FBOs anyway). Drivers that do support
  surfaceless contexts behave exactly as before, GBM keeps failing instead of using a pbuffer.
- AcceleratedSurface::RenderTarget::createSkiaSurfaceForFramebuffer(): do not dereference a missing Skia GL context, report it and leave the
  Skia surface empty.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLContext.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLContext.cpp
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLContext.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/egl/GLContext.cpp
@@ -230,6 +230,14 @@
     return makeUnique<GLContext>(display, context, surface, config);
 }
 
+// Some vendor EGL implementations (Broadcom/Nexus V3D, e.g. VU+ Ultimo 4K) offer neither EGL_KHR_surfaceless_context nor
+// EGL_KHR_surfaceless_opengl: no context can be made current without a surface there.
+static bool eglSupportsSurfacelessContexts(GLDisplay& display)
+{
+    const char* extensions = eglQueryString(display.eglDisplay(), EGL_EXTENSIONS);
+    return GLContext::isExtensionSupported(extensions, "EGL_KHR_surfaceless_context") || GLContext::isExtensionSupported(extensions, "EGL_KHR_surfaceless_opengl");
+}
+
 std::unique_ptr<GLContext> GLContext::createOffscreenContext(GLDisplay& display, Target target, EGLContext sharingContext)
 {
     if (auto context = createSurfacelessContext(display, target, sharingContext))
@@ -246,9 +254,13 @@
     case Target::GBM:
 #endif
     case Target::Surfaceless:
-        // Do not fallback to pbuffers.
-        RELEASE_LOG_INFO(Compositing, "Could not create EGL surfaceless context: %s.", lastErrorString());
-        return nullptr;
+        // Do not fallback to pbuffers, unless the EGL implementation cannot do surfaceless contexts at all: then a
+        // pbuffer is the only way to get an offscreen context, and without one nothing can be rendered.
+        if (target != Target::Surfaceless || eglSupportsSurfacelessContexts(display)) {
+            RELEASE_LOG_INFO(Compositing, "Could not create EGL surfaceless context: %s.", lastErrorString());
+            return nullptr;
+        }
+        break;
     default:
         break;
     }
diff --git a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
@@ -161,7 +161,12 @@
     glGetIntegerv(GL_STENCIL_BITS, &stencilBits);
 
     auto& display = PlatformDisplay::sharedDisplay();
-    GLContext::ScopedGLContextCurrent scopedCurrent(*display.skiaGLContext());
+    auto* skiaGLContext = display.skiaGLContext();
+    if (!skiaGLContext) {
+        LOG_ERROR("AcceleratedSurface has no Skia GL context for the render target");
+        return;
+    }
+    GLContext::ScopedGLContextCurrent scopedCurrent(*skiaGLContext);
 
     GrGLFramebufferInfo framebufferInfo;
     framebufferInfo.fFBOID = fbo;
